    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0321" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/366</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Cork</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Frost</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cork</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Queenstown</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-02-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 1.10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cunarder <hi rendition="#italic">Laconia</hi> torpedoed, sunk 10.50, 25th, 150
                    miles west Fastnet. Details not yet known. Two hundred and seventy-eight
                    survivors will land here to-day, time uncertain. It is known that there are some
                    missing and one dead. Will cable details at earliest moment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
